{{Item|Jacob's Ticket}}s are items that can be spent with {{NPCSprite|Anita}} to buy items to help build farms, as well as chips that grant {{Stat|Crop Fortune}} for the active crop during the contest and increased experience gain for [[Farming Tools]]. They are also used to buy {{stat|Farming Fortune}} boosts and increase players' {{Skill|Farming}} level cap to 60 (LX).

Turbo-Crop books are [[Enchanted Book]]s with enchantments that grant the player 5 of the corresponding {{Stat|Crop Fortune}} per level, up to 5. Level 4 and 5 Turbo-Crop enchantments require a having earned a {{Medal|BRONZE}} and {{Medal|SILVER}} in their crop, respectively, otherwise they act as if the player didn't have the Turbo-Crop enchantment at all. The player will always get a book for the crop whose contest they participated in. The books may also appear as a reward from the {{NPCSprite|Librarian}} visitor on {{zone|The Garden}}.

The amount of [[Bits]] earned from contests is multiplied by the player's Bits Multiplier, based on their [[Fame Rank]].

Earning a {{Medal|GOLD}} medal allows the player to increase their {{Skill|Farming}} level cap by one per crop they earned a {{Medal|GOLD}} medal in, up to 60 (LX).

The {{Medal|PLATINUM}} and {{Medal|DIAMOND}} tiers do not have their own medals, but rather give the player additional medals and other rewards as seen in the table above. Reaching the {{Medal|PLATINUM}} or {{Medal|DIAMOND}} bracket in all crops will also reward the player with unique [[emblem]]s.

== Previous and Upcoming Events ==
<!--For the time of Jacob events, please visit [[Jacob's Farming Contest/Events]]. (outdated)-->
Current and upcoming Jacob's Farming Contests can be viewed the tab list, Jacob's menu, as well as the SkyBlock [[Calendar]].

<!--== Strategy ==
To place in a Farming Contest usually requires a large size of farms in the player's [[The Garden|Garden]] and/or hundreds of [[Farming Fortune]] after the 0.18 update. Using the tools provided by [[Anita]] can help build farms faster because the default plots are too insufficient and slow to farm, despite the fact that some of the items are not marketable and will need to be procured through their intended purchase method (which requires placement in Farming Contests), or through direct trade with another player. If needed, get a [[Builder's Ruler]] instead of a [[Builder's Wand]]. The Builder's Ruler is much powerful and inexpensive compared to the Builder's Wand. [[Minions]] will not count towards the contest, despite giving full {{Skillname|Farming}} XP, unless the player manually breaks crops planted by the minion, but using minions is inefficient either way due to Farming Fortune being removed from private islands.

With an enough size farm of the specific crops in the Garden, a player will be able to farm for the full 20 minutes of the Contest. This should be a player's first goal if they wish to place {{Medal|GOLD}} in the Contest.

Farming on the player's [[Private Island]] is no longer viable for contests due to Farming Fortune being disabled there. Farming in the [[Hub]] or [[Farm]], while it still grants Farming Fortune, is not recommended for contests as the crops generally don't regrow fast enough, there may be competition from other players, and the farm layouts are not optimal to maximize <abbr title="BPS">Breaks Per Second</abbr> without lane switches causing delays.

[[Wheat]] can be farmed easily by all players as it is the default crop unlocked in the Garden. To be compacted, both [[Enchanted Wheat]] and [[Enchanted Seeds]] should be placed into the player's Personal Compactor.

[[Potato|Potatoes]] and [[Carrot|Carrots]] are best farmed with the Garden farm, but using a flat layer of Dirt with a few breaks for water also works.

[[Nether Wart]] is best farmed the same way as Carrots and Potatoes, with [[Soul Sand]] instead of Dirt, and needing no Water, so a flat layer with no breaks is possible. Farming in the [[Crimson Isle]] can be an alternative choice, but it requires {{Skill|Combat 22}} and is probably not optimal for contests, being a public island.

[[Pumpkin|Pumpkins]] and [[Melon|Melons]] will need a farm on the player's Garden. Because of the need for a Stem to grow the crop, Pumpkins and Melons are best farmed in straight lines, perhaps two at a time to increase yield speed.

[[Sugar Cane]] needs to be farmed in the Garden to be effective, because the [[Mushroom Desert|Mushroom Desert's]] Sugar Cane spawn rate is too low and Garden crops have an increase in growing speed. There are various ways to farm Sugar Cane, with some players preferring to maximize space usage with a design closer to a Wheat farm, and other players preferring the harvesting speed efficiency of the straight line Pumpkin and Melon farm.

If players are online and do not wish to participate, or know they will not score highly in the currently selected crops, farming at least 100 of the crop will give the player 1 [[Jacob's Ticket]] as a participation prize, as well as increasing the amount of participants in a given contest, allowing more players who wish to participate to score higher. Collaboration can make the game easier for everyone.

=== Useful Enchantments ===
Scoring high in a Farming Contest is much easier with good [[Enchantments]] on your farming tool. [[Hoe]]s can have many useful enchantments.

{{ench|Replenish}} automatically replants crops when broken. This is unavoidable if you want to achieve a high score on Wheat, Carrot, Potato, Cocoa Beans or Nether Wart because replanting them even with a [[Basket of Seeds]] takes a lot time. Note that if you are using a Personal Compactor, you should have at least a [[Small Agronomy Sack]] to prevent the compactor from compacting the seeds before they can be replanted by Replenish.

{{ench|Harvesting}} for [[Hoes]] or {{ench|Sunder}} for [[Axes]] increases your {{Stat|Farming Fortune}}, which affects a player's chance to get more crops.

Every {{ench|Turbo-Crop}} Enchantment increases your {{Stat|Farming Fortune}} by {{Green|+5}} per level when breaking its specific crop. Turbo-Crop [[Enchanted Book]]s can be obtained by winning any medal in a Farming Contest, or from the [[Bazaar]].-->

== Tips ==
*It is possible to kill [[Pest]]s during contests, as well as prepare up to {{Green|20}} Pests ahead of time ({{Green|8}} on the Garden and {{Green|12}} in {{Item|Vermin Trap}}s) and kill them as soon as the contest starts in order to achieve much higher scores.
** Furthermore, a player can also prepare all [[Greenhouse]] plots with the crop that will be in the contest. This allows the player to instantly get a high amount of crops depending on their [[Greenhouse Upgrades]] and {{Stat|Fmf}}.

== Trivia ==
*Contest brackets each include one additional player on top of the normal percentage, so players may score in a higher bracket if they were the one closest to it.
*When starting a contest or warping within the last 3 seconds of a contest, {{NPCSprite|Jacob}} may be unable to figure out the player's placing. However, the score will be calculated correctly regardless.
*The chat message may report the wrong bracket if it was very close and changed last second. {{NPCSprite|Jacob}} will tell players the actual bracket they placed in when talking to him.
*If there is a Jacob's Contest ongoing, scheduled server restarts will be delayed until 20 seconds after it is over. However, unlike [[Dungeons]] and [[Kuudra]], game update restarts are not delayed.

